\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(NSFileHandle *)\b fileHandleForReading\
\fs14\
\b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns an NSFileHandle that accepts messages that read pipe data: \b availableData\b0 , \b readDataToEndOfFile\b0 , \b readDataOfLength:\b0 . You don\'27t need to send \b closeFile\b0  to this object or explicitly release after you\'27re finished using it. This descriptor represented by this object is deleted and the object itself is automatically deallocated when the NSPipe is deallocated.\
\fs14\
